  "about": "Every book cut-out. Edit the anchors; never the boxes. resolve_crops.py finds each anchor's text with pdftotext -bbox, snaps outwards to the element's full ink (fills, rules, edge bars) on the 300 dpi render, adds the 8 px margin, and writes page and box (pixels at 300 dpi, [x0, y0, x1, y1]). bookPage is the men's page as brief 5.2 indexes it; the edition's own page is derived from it (women's = men's up to p42, then + 3). Modes: element (anchors, snapped, margin), day-page (a day page's header and session: the text column's width plus 12 pt, from 16 pt above anchor.first down to the last anchor, snapped), page (the whole trimmed page), cover-front (the front panel of a cover wrap, trimmed).",
